NAME
    printenv - print the inherited environment

SYNOPSIS
    printenv

DESCRIPTION
    Prints the environment variables this program inherited from the shell,
    one NAME=VALUE per line. The shell exports its environment (the vars set
    with `set`, plus PATH) to every command it spawns, so `printenv` shows
    what a spawned program sees.

    A pipeline stage like any other, so it can be filtered:
    `printenv | grep PATH`.

EXAMPLES
    printenv
    set FOO=bar
    printenv | grep FOO

SEE ALSO
    env, set, unset
